+// GC_CUTCORNERCACHE. On a cut layer a convex corner is fixed when some fixed
+// cut rectangle of the net has its corner, in the corner's direction, at the
+// corner point (isCornerOverlap). Scanning the rectangle list for every
+// corner makes the pass O(corners x fixed cut rectangles) per layer, which is
+// quadratic on power/ground via arrays. With the gate on, the corner points of
+// the layer's fixed rectangles are put in four sets (one per direction) the
+// first time the layer is visited, and each corner is one lookup.
+//
+// Equivalence: isCornerOverlap(corner, rect) holds exactly when the corner
+// point getNextEdge()->low() equals (xh, yh) of rect for NE, (xh, yl) for SE,
+// (xl, yl) for SW and (xl, yh) for NW, and never for another direction. The
+// set for a direction holds exactly those points of the same
+// getRectangles(true)[layer] list, which the corner pass does not modify, so
+// membership is the predicate "some rectangle matches" and the fixed flag is
+// the same. Gate read once from the environment: unset or 0 = original.
+bool cutCornerCacheEnabled()
+{
+  static const bool enabled = [] {
+    const char* v = std::getenv("GC_CUTCORNERCACHE");
+    return v != nullptr && v[0] != '\0' && v[0] != '0';
+  }();
+  return enabled;
+}
